<!--
    Apple unified-logging call sites (`option oslog on|off`) and Mach-O
    literal pools other than `__cstring`.

    Issue: an `os_log` macro packs its arguments into a stack buffer (summary
    byte, count byte, then per argument a descriptor byte, a size byte and the
    value) and calls `_os_log_impl(&__dso_handle, log, type, fmt, buf, size)`.
    On iOS 16.4.1 trustd every log statement read
    `v1 = 0x4000100; v8 = v2; _os_log_impl(0x100000000,v3,0,s_10006c0cf,&v1,8);`:
    the format string in `__TEXT,__oslogstring` printed as its symbol, the
    arguments were raw buffer stores, and the dso was a bare address.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 (the Mach-O loader's section classification,
    `kuna-analysis/src/loader/format/macho.rs`: an `S_CSTRING_LITERALS` section
    is read-only data) and P9 presentation (`p9_emit/kuna_oslog.rs`).

    P0 assertion: `option oslog on|off` (default on), a print-time gate.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture. Both passes load the
    real arm64 Mach-O fixture `macho_oslog_arm64` (built from `macho_oslog.c`
    with clang's `__builtin_os_log_format`, see the fixtures README; the format
    strings are in `__TEXT,__oslogstring`). `_log_code` @0x100000418 logs one
    int, `_log_pair` @0x1000004a8 a long and a string (the string written as an
    unaligned 8-byte store), `_log_plain` @0x100000600 no arguments.

    Pass 1 (`option oslog off`, the BUG for the call shape): the format string
    is a literal (the literal-pool fix is unconditional), the header and value
    stores print and the call passes `0x100000000,...,&v1,8`. Pass 2
    (`option oslog on`, the default, the FIX): the call prints
    `_os_log_impl(&__mh_execute_header,a0,0x10,"failed to read parents: %d",a1)`
    with no buffer stores.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
